%U A401979 568375,847454,1261933,1889545,2865524,4428135,6996281,11297774,18575426,30909745
%N A401979 Number of tilings of a strip of length n using squares (length 1) and dominoes (length 2) such that the number of dominoes is a Fibonacci number.
%F A401979 a(n) = Sum_{k>=0, 2*F(k)<=n} binomial(n-F(k), F(k)), where the sum is over distinct Fibonacci numbers F(k), including 0.
%F A401979 G.f.: A(x) = Sum_{d in F} x^(2*d)/(1-x)^(d+1), where F = {0,1,2,3,5,8,13,...}.
%e A401979 For n = 4, you can use 0, 1, or 2 dominoes. 0 dominoes: all squares, 1 tiling. 1 domino: 3 possible tilings. 2 dominos: 1 possible tiling. This leads to a total of 5 possible tilings.
%K A401979 nonn,new
